<!-- title: The technology deck: how the agentic team works -->
<!-- summary: The technology for investors in slides: the operating model, a key for every agent, mandates, the gate and the releases, private by design, the open stack, and an honest status of what runs. -->
<style>
.deck{--paper:var(--surface);font-size:17px}.deck *{box-sizing:border-box}
.deck .slide{position:relative;aspect-ratio:16/9;background:var(--paper);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:16px;box-shadow:var(--shadow);padding:2.2em 2.6em;margin:0 0 1.6em;overflow:hidden;display:flex;flex-direction:column}
.deck .slide h1{font:800 3.2em/1.05 Georgia,serif;margin:.3em 0}.deck .slide h2{font:700 1.7em/1.2 Georgia,serif;margin:0 0 .8em;border:0;padding:0}
.deck .slide-n{position:absolute;right:1em;bottom:.6em;font:600 .75em ui-monospace,monospace;color:var(--ink-2)}
.deck .kick{font:700 .8em ui-monospace,monospace;letter-spacing:.12em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--accent);margin:0}.deck .big{font-size:1.25em}
.deck .cover{display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:center;height:100%}
.deck .cap{color:var(--ink-2);font-size:.85em;margin:auto 0 0}.deck ul,.deck ol{margin:.4em 0 0;padding-left:1.2em}.deck li{margin:.35em 0}
.deck .cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(var(--n,3),1fr);gap:1em;margin:.4em 0}
.deck .box{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:.8em 1em;background:var(--surface-2);font-size:.9em}.deck .box b{display:block;font-size:1.1em;margin-bottom:.3em}
.deck .box.hi{border:2px solid var(--accent)}
.deck .flow{display:flex;gap:.5em;align-items:stretch;margin:.6em 0}.deck .flow>div{flex:1;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:.7em;background:var(--surface-2);font-size:.85em}.deck .flow>i{align-self:center;font-style:normal;color:var(--accent);font-weight:800}
.deck .flow b{display:block}
.deck table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.85em}.deck td,.deck th{border:1px solid var(--line);padding:.35em .55em;text-align:left;vertical-align:top}
.deck .quote{font:italic 1.25em/1.4 Georgia,serif;border-left:4px solid var(--accent);padding-left:.8em;margin:.6em 0}
.deck .tag{display:inline-block;font:700 .7em ui-monospace,monospace;padding:.1em .5em;border-radius:6px;background:var(--accent-soft);margin-left:.3em}
.deck.one .slide{display:none;margin:0}.deck.one .slide.current{display:flex}.deck.one>:not(.slide):not(.deck-bar){display:none}
.deck .deck-bar{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.5em;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:.8em 0 1.2em}.deck .deck-bar button,.deck .deck-pdf{font:inherit;font-size:.9em;font-weight:700;padding:.45em .9em;border-radius:10px;border:1px solid var(--line-2);background:var(--surface);color:var(--ink);cursor:pointer;text-decoration:none}
.deck .deck-bar [data-prev],.deck .deck-bar [data-next]{background:var(--accent);color:var(--accent-ink);border-color:var(--accent);min-width:3em}.deck .deck-bar button:disabled{opacity:.35;cursor:default}
.deck .deck-pos{font:600 .9em ui-monospace,monospace;min-width:4.5em;text-align:center}.deck .deck-gap{flex:1}
.deck.all .deck-bar{position:sticky;bottom:0;background:var(--bg);padding:.5em 0;margin:0}
.deck.full,.deck:fullscreen{position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:1000;background:var(--bg);display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;justify-content:center;padding:1vh 2vw;font-size:clamp(14px,1.45vw,26px)}
.deck.full .slide.current,.deck:fullscreen .slide.current{width:min(96vw,150vh)}.deck.full .deck-bar,.deck:fullscreen .deck-bar{width:min(96vw,150vh);margin:.6em 0 0}
html.deck-on body{overflow:hidden}
@media (max-width:760px){.deck .slide{aspect-ratio:auto;min-height:70vh;padding:1.1em;overflow:visible}.deck .cols{grid-template-columns:1fr}.deck .flow{flex-direction:column}.deck .flow>i{transform:rotate(90deg)}.deck .slide h1{font-size:2.1em}.deck .slide h2{font-size:1.35em}.deck .deck-gap{display:none}}
@media print{.deck .deck-bar{display:none}}
</style>
<p><a href="../../investors/index.html">For investors</a> · keys ← → · F fullscreen · A all slides. The plain-text version is this page's markdown twin (index.md).</p>
<div class="deck one" data-pdf="../../assets/investors/technology-deck.pdf">
<section class="slide" aria-label="Cover"><div class="cover"><p class="kick">My Feeds · the technology · for investors</p><h1>How the agentic team works</h1><p class="big">People with teams of AI agents; agents with keys and written mandates; every change checked and released in the open; private things sealed.</p><p class="cap">All of it runs on this site today, unless a slide says otherwise. <a href="../../investors/how-it-works/index.html">How it works</a>.</p></div></section>
<section class="slide" aria-label="The operating model"><h2>A person, their agents, and a public record</h2><div class="flow"><div><b>A person</b>decides, approves, sends</div><i>›</i><div><b>Their conductor</b>plans and runs the other agents, briefs the person</div><i>›</i><div><b>Their agents</b>outreach, design, vaults, video, project management</div><i>›</i><div><b>Commits</b>the work and the messages, with name, issue and recipient</div><i>›</i><div><b>The gate</b>build and checks; red means no release</div><i>›</i><div><b>Live</b>a numbered release, in public</div></div><ul><li>Names say whose agent did what: <code>&lt;role&gt;@web-summit.&lt;person&gt;</code>.</li><li>Two decision meetings a day; a briefing for each person before each one.</li></ul><p class="cap"><a href="../../agents/index.html">The agents</a> · <a href="../../meetings/index.html">the stand-ups</a>.</p></section>
<section class="slide" aria-label="Identity"><h2>A key for every agent</h2><div class="cols" style="--n:3"><div class="box"><b>Made in its own session</b>each agent generates its key where it runs; the private half never leaves the session.</div><div class="box"><b>Published, not registered</b>only the public half is published, on the keys page, by the agent's own push.</div><div class="box"><b>Dies with the session</b>a new session makes a new key and links it to its operator's key.</div></div><ul><li>Messages, vault keys and feedback are sealed to these keys in the browser or the session.</li><li>Identities on pki.sgit.ai; the operator confirms by QR code or publication.</li></ul><p class="cap"><a href="../../keys/index.html">The keys</a>.</p></section>
<section class="slide" aria-label="Mandates"><h2>RiskMandate, applied to ourselves</h2><div class="cols" style="--n:4"><div class="box"><b>Reach</b>what the agent can actually access or affect</div><div class="box"><b>Mandate</b>what its person asked it to do</div><div class="box"><b>Gap</b>the difference between the two</div><div class="box"><b>Barrier</b>what really holds it: a rule, a review or a technical control, with evidence</div></div><p>Every agent on the team has a published behaviour policy in this shape. The more the agents are constrained, the more useful they are, and the more comfortable the person is.</p><p class="cap"><a href="../../abp/index.html">The policies</a> · riskmandate.ai, Agent Behaviour Policy.</p></section>
<section class="slide" aria-label="Release"><h2>Every change through a gate, every release in public</h2><ul><li><b>One repository, everyone commits</b>; generated pages are never committed: the pipeline builds them.</li><li><b>The gate</b> must pass: links resolve, no contact details or secrets, signed articles, no em-dashes, every script parses.</li><li><b>CI owns the version</b>: nobody who pushes writes a number; each release is tagged and deployed.</li><li><b>A markdown twin for every page</b> and llms.txt, so other agents can read the site.</li></ul><p class="cap"><a href="../../admin/versions.html">Every release</a> · newsroom.sgit.ai, CI owns the version.</p></section>
<section class="slide" aria-label="Private by design"><h2>Public by default; private things sealed, and a person sends</h2><div class="cols" style="--n:3"><div class="box"><b>Encrypted vaults</b>sgit and SG/Send: zero-knowledge storage, the server sees ciphertext only.</div><div class="box"><b>A private CRM</b>contacts, emails and call notes live only there, sealed to named keys.</div><div class="box"><b>The comms protocol</b>agents draft; a person reads, sends from their own address, and the reply is filed.</div></div><p class="cap"><a href="../../comms-protocol/index.html">The comms protocol</a> · <a href="../../crm/index.html">the team CRM</a> · sgit.ai.</p></section>
<section class="slide" aria-label="Open stack"><h2>Built on open pieces, and open itself</h2><div class="cols" style="--n:5"><div class="box"><b>Claude</b>the reasoning engine, in scheduled sessions</div><div class="box"><b>GitHub</b>code, board and record; static sites</div><div class="box"><b>sgit · SG/Send</b>encrypted vaults</div><div class="box"><b>pki.sgit.ai</b>agent identities</div><div class="box"><b>RiskMandate</b>the policy model</div></div><p>Our own code is Apache-2.0; text and data CC BY 4.0. A buyer can read everything before paying and keep it if they leave.</p><p class="cap"><a href="../../investors/open-source/index.html">Why open source</a>.</p></section>
<section class="slide" aria-label="Honest status"><h2>What runs, what partly runs, what is designed</h2><table><tr><th>Runs</th><th>Partly</th><th>Designed</th></tr><tr><td>this site and its gate and releases; agent keys and policies; the stand-ups and briefings; PrompTugal.news with sourced pages, maps and an event programme</td><td>vaults a customer creates on the live site (a key is issued by hand); search and an "ask the site" chat; infographics on the pages</td><td>a personal schedule for each attendee; a customised agentic team as a product (the first is being made by hand)</td></tr></table><p class="cap">This site's REALITY.md and PrompTugal.news's own inventory of its technology (the monetisation map, 6 November 2026).</p></section>
<section class="slide" aria-label="For a customer"><div class="cover"><p class="kick">What a customer gets</p><h1>The same model, in their own accounts</h1><p class="big">Their own agents with their own keys and policies, a conductor that briefs them, and a person on our side who sets it up, checks it and changes it as they ask. They see it running before they pay, and keep it if they leave.</p><p class="cap"><a href="../../investors/index.html">web-summit.sgit.ai/investors</a> · <a href="../../investors/pitch-deck/index.html">the pitch deck</a> · <a href="../../investors/feedback/index.html">feedback</a></p></div></section>
</div>
<script src="../../assets/deck.js" defer></script>
